🧠 What is a Custom Module?

👉 A custom module = module YOU create manually

Not from registry, not external — your own reusable code

🔹 Definition

A custom module is a user-defined Terraform module stored locally or in Git

🔥 Types of Modules (Correct Classification)

Now full picture:

Root Module → your main project
Custom Module (Local Module) → created by you
Remote/Public Module → from registry/Git
📁 Example (Your Project)

👉 These are custom modules you built:

modules/
 ├── vpc/
 ├── nlb/
 ├── route53/
 ├── eks/

✔️ All are custom modules

🔧 How Custom Module is Used
module "vpc" {
  source = "./modules/vpc"
  vpc_cidr = "10.10.0.0/16"
}

👉 ./modules/vpc = local path
👉 That means custom module

🔄 Custom Module Workflow
You create module → Define variables → Write resources → Output values
        ↓
Root module calls it → Pass inputs → Gets outputs
🔥 Why Custom Modules?
✅ Control
Full customization
No dependency on external modules
✅ Standardization
Same infra pattern across projects
✅ Security
No external code risk
⚠️ When NOT to Use Custom Modules?

👉 Use public modules when:

Common infra (VPC, EKS)
Want faster setup

Example:

source = "terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws"
🔥 Custom vs Public Module
Feature	Custom Module	Public Module
Control	Full	Limited
Setup time	Medium	Fast
Flexibility	High	Depends
Maintenance	You manage	Community
